claim: "The person portrayed by actor Micah Hauptman in \"Everest\" is a mountaineer. So is the Canadian who first climbed the Seven Summits."
evidences (the complete set of findings collected so far, oldest first):
[
 {
  "finding": {
   "question": "Who is the character portrayed by actor Micah Hauptman in the movie Everest and is this character a mountaineer?",
   "answer": "INSUFFICIENT",
   "source": "",
   "excerpt": "",
   "stance": "INSUFFICIENT"
  },
  "passage": ""
 },
 {
  "finding": {
   "question": "Who was the first Canadian to climb the Seven Summits and is this person a mountaineer?",
   "answer": "INSUFFICIENT",
   "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seven_Summits",
   "excerpt": "The Seven Summits are the highest mountains on each of the seven traditional continents. On 30 April 1985, Richard Bass became the first climber to reach the summit of all seven.",
   "stance": "INSUFFICIENT"
  },
  "passage": "Title: List of climbers and mountaineers\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_climbers_and_mountaineers\nExcerpt: This is a list of climbers and mountaineers who are notable for their activities in mountaineering (including alpine climbing), rock climbing (including aid climbing, free climbing, bouldering, speed climbing and competition climbing) or in ice climbing (including mixed climbing).\n\nTitle: Seven Summits\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seven_Summits\nExcerpt: The Seven Summits are the highest mountains on each of the seven traditional continents. On 30 April 1985, Richard Bass became the first climber to reach the summit of all seven.\nIn January 2023, Climbing said \"Today, the Seven Summits are a relatively common—almost cliché—tour of each continent's highest peak\", and while reaching the peak of the \"Seven Summits\" is no longer considered a significant achievement amongst mountaineers, it remains a popular challenge for \"adventure mountaineers\" using expedition climbing techniques.\n\nTitle: Volcanic Seven Summits\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volcanic_Seven_Summits\nExcerpt: The Volcanic Seven Summits are the highest volcanoes on each of the seven continents, just as the Seven Summits are the highest peaks on each of the seven continents. Two of the Volcanic Seven Summits are also on the Seven Summits list. Kilimanjaro and Mount Elbrus, which were formed volcanically, are the highest peaks of their respective continents.\n\nTitle: List of Mount Everest records\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Mount_Everest_records\nExcerpt: This article lists different records related to Mount Everest. One of the most commonly sought after records is a \"summit\", meaning to reach the highest elevation point on Mount Everest."
 }
]

